WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:06.240
Grigori Gusakov and Anatoly Korneev, both
aged ten, tiptoed through the deep, dark woods

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.410
bordering their quaint Russian village of
Obrechennyy.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:14.990
The year was 1990, a turbulent time for the
people of Russia, seeing as the Soviet Union

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.270
was on the precipice of collapse.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:23.590
But for these two young boys, global geopolitics
was the last thing on their minds.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:30.880
They were too busy hunting for the legendary,
monstrous witch known only as Baba Yaga.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.420
For those in our audience who grew up in Eastern
Europe, or those at least decently familiar

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:40.850
with Slavic Folklore and/or the John Wick
film series, mention of the name Baba Yaga

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.989
likely sends a slight chill down your spine.

00:00:43.989 --> 00:00:46.309
And if it doesn’t, just wait.

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:50.120
By the end of this video, you’ll be afraid
to go into the woods alone.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:55.329
Not that going with others would save you,
as poor little Grigori and Anatoly were about

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:57.440
to find out the hard way…

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.940
They forged on through those witchy woods.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.280
By our standards, the boys were tough and
headstrong.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.280
After all, the Russian wilderness could be
a brutal place to grow up, and in a town like

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:12.920
Obrechennyy, the old ways of stoicism and
perseverance were prized over fear and caution.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.500
All except for one particular area: The Supernatural.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.130
Like many small villages all over the world
at every point in history, Obrechennyy had

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:24.649
its fair share of local superstitions.

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:29.259
Chief among them was the belief that the local
forest was enchanted, and that when people

00:01:29.259 --> 00:01:33.399
wandered in among the trees, many of them
would never return.

00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:38.329
They’d fall into the gnarled clutches of
the carnivorous witch Baba Yaga, and their

00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:43.500
bones would lay among the roots and dead leaves
until they someday crumbled into dust.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.420
It was starting to get dark out.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.420
The air was cold and thick.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:50.240
When the two boys had first set off, it’d
been with the intention of proving their mettle

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.590
among the other local children.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:57.149
They didn’t fear Baba Yaga; the old witch
in the woods was just another fairy story

00:01:57.149 --> 00:02:00.950
meant to frighten children, and they weren’t
children anymore.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:04.520
Though they would never live to be men.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.270
It wasn’t long before they were beyond the
point of no return.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.759
Which way was out, and which way was further
in?

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:14.920
It hardly mattered anymore, as carrion birds
cawed far above.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:19.450
The bravado that put them here was starting
to falter now, but neither dared show it.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.430
They’d rather be put in mortal peril than
show fear in front of one another.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.629
Was something moving in the distant shadows?

00:02:25.629 --> 00:02:30.900
A thin, twisted, human figure, impossible
to make out save for the faint glow of its

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.840
eyes in the gathering dark?

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:37.651
They couldn’t tell what was real and what
was their mind playing cruel tricks on them.

00:02:37.651 --> 00:02:42.550
A hoarse whisper issued through the brittle
trees in the moments that followed.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:49.230
It was an ancient voice, a voice that had
echoed in the nightmares of generations, a

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.099
voice that had seen centuries.

00:02:52.099 --> 00:02:57.610
It spoke in an older Russian dialect than
either of the young boys could understand,

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:04.390
but somehow, the essence of its message still
rung clear in their hearts and minds.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:08.939
“Welcome, little children, to my forest.

00:03:08.939 --> 00:03:12.730
Here, your lives are forfeit.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:15.760
You are my property.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:25.500
I look forward to chewing the tender meat
off your young bones.”

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.189
That was all they needed to hear to start
running.

00:03:28.189 --> 00:03:34.200
Gregori and Anatoly turned and fled, screaming
for help, into the darkness of the forest.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.080
Both gasped as they ran through what seemed
to be a giant spider web.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:44.180
They spat and spluttered, trying to swat away
the silky strands as they ran from the voice.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:48.860
Little did they know, what they’d just run
through was no spider web.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:52.370
They tried to press on, but their footsteps
slowed.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.319
The forest was changing around them.

00:03:55.319 --> 00:03:57.900
Twisting, shifting, sparkling.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:04.459
What had seemed terrifying before was suddenly
oddly...beautiful.

00:04:04.459 --> 00:04:08.860
The two boys just stood and watched as the
forest turned into a gorgeous Technicolor

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:13.400
light show, unlike anything they’d ever
seen before.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.709
Strange figures hopped and danced through
the foliage.

00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:19.220
One tall figure approached them out of the
trees.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.940
A beautiful, fair-haired maiden.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.520
The two boys were entranced by her.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.150
Their hearts were filled with pure golden
light.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.199
Why were they running before?

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:30.870
They couldn’t even remember.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:36.930
They just smiled as the woman approached them
in her long, flowing dress, smiling back.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:39.930
She was like something out of a fairy tale.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.440
They didn’t react.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:47.180
They didn’t even realize what was happening,
as the jaws of the horrible, ancient old crone

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.600
closed around their skulls for the last time.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.850
Grigori and Anatoly were never seen again.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:58.720
Just another two children gone missing in
the woods, the latest entries on a long list

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.130
of tragedies to hit the village of Obrechennyy.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:04.940
But they were also the straws that broke the
camel’s back.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:08.580
The villagers were sick of living in fear
under the fabled witch.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.970
They would have their revenge.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:14.480
The men of the village gathered up their weapons
and formed a hunting party.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:18.600
Guns, torches, knives, axes, and fury.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:22.890
They would slay the beast that had taken so
many of their friends and their children in

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.120
the woods.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:29.630
As soon as their forces were assembled, they
charged into the forest, looking for blood.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:34.130
With their numerical advantage and single-minded
determination, it didn’t take them long

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:36.380
to find the monster in the woods.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:41.960
She was every bit as hideous and nightmarish
as they’d anticipated: A gnarled, snarling

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:45.630
crone, with long, clawed fingers and dirty
fangs.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:50.360
They got her in their sights and prepared
to open fire, but none of them were ready

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:53.360
for Baba Yaga’s counteroffensive.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:57.979
She moved like a leaf in a strong wind, swift
and effortless.

00:05:57.979 --> 00:06:02.090
The men who’d made the mistake of getting
too close to her with knives and axes tasted

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.789
her terrible wrath.

00:06:03.789 --> 00:06:06.160
She tore through them with claws like iron.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.050
Sank her fangs into their flesh.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.220
Lifted and tossed them like rag dolls.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.419
How could she be so fast and so strong?

00:06:14.419 --> 00:06:16.419
The men were terrified.

00:06:16.419 --> 00:06:18.280
This was no mere woman.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:23.430
It was a true monster, squeezed into a barely
human form.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:28.280
By the time the creature was finally incapacitated,
it’d taken countless bullets and strikes.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:32.440
How any creature could survive such an assault
was unimaginable.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.450
Several members of the hunting party were
dead by this point.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.220
Others had been overtaken by a strange form
of madness.

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:43.540
A couple of them had been given to constant
giggling fits or were speaking long strings

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.270
of nonsense.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:49.380
Others had been rendered entirely catatonic
by the experience.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:53.130
It was clear that the witch had powers beyond
their understanding.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:57.879
They needed to return it to the village and
destroy it as quickly as possible.

00:06:57.879 --> 00:07:01.039
The monster was bound and dragged back to
Obrechennyy.

00:07:01.039 --> 00:07:04.729
After seeing how it bewitched some of the
men, they avoided direct contact whenever

00:07:04.729 --> 00:07:05.830
possible.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:10.260
They would do everything they could to see
justice done.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:13.539
Of course, there would be no due process for
Baba Yaga.

00:07:13.539 --> 00:07:17.370
The violence that had erupted in the forest
was more than enough proof to justify the

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.639
beast’s immediate death sentence.

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:23.569
The local priest gave a prayer - though he
remarked that he was sure this monster was

00:07:23.569 --> 00:07:27.460
the creation and servant of the devil - and
the execution commenced.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:32.900
A local used a blessed sword, anointed with
holy water, to hack off the Baba Yaga’s

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:33.900
head.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:38.190
Its body was shot several times for good measure,
and it was finally doused in gasoline and

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.580
set on fire.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:44.729
The remains were buried just outside the village
limits, hoping that the Baba Yaga’s evil

00:07:44.729 --> 00:07:48.500
wouldn’t continue to haunt their town, even
in death.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:53.460
Isolated villages in the Russian steppe aren’t
famous for their communication with outsiders,

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:58.800
especially back in 1990, when the Soviet Union
was still clinging on to control and the internet

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:00.270
was still in its infancy.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:05.000
It took a few weeks for the news of a village
capturing its so-called local witch to reach

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.150
the SCP Foundation.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:11.659
After closely studying the peculiar disappearance
records in the area, they sent over a detachment

00:08:11.659 --> 00:08:16.699
of field agents to investigate, and perhaps
conduct a few interviews with the locals.

00:08:16.699 --> 00:08:21.740
They had no way of knowing there wouldn’t
be any left by the time they arrived.

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:25.710
When the field agents reached Obrechennyy,
it was already a ghost town.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:30.860
Not a single survivor was found, only the
evidence of fresh carnage.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.110
Desiccated bodies were found in some of the
village’s houses.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.120
In others, only body parts.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:41.270
A hole in the ground next to the village seemed
to show evidence of some subterranean creature

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:44.050
clawing its way back up to the top.

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:48.230
Whatever this creature was, it’d clearly
crawled back up from the earth and exacted

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:51.340
bloody revenge against those who had buried
it.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:55.420
Blood trails from some of the bodies leading
back into the woods made it clear where the

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:59.360
creature had fled to after massacring the
entire village.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:04.900
Given the sudden increase in the situation’s
severity, Mobile Task Force Epsilon-6, aka

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:08.880
The Village Idiots, were brought in to apprehend
the fugitive witch.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:14.530
But much like the literal village idiots that’d
come before them, this MTF had no idea what

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:15.650
they were up against.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:20.180
They entered the forest outside Obrechennyy
with superior tactics and weaponry to the

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:23.090
villagers, with orders to contain the creature
at all costs.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:27.730
They didn’t exactly know what they were
searching for in the dark amongst the trees,

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:32.410
but when the first operatives laid eyes on
the twisted old crone, they almost reflexively

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:33.960
relaxed their guard.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:39.180
For some of the Village Idiots, this would
be the last mistake they ever made.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.520
Some of the operatives began to feel funny.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:45.730
Much like Grigori, Anatoly, and some members
of the hunting party, they began to see the

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.270
forest warping and shifting around them.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:53.490
They giggled at all the funny colors, and
sighed, feeling an overwhelming sense of calmness

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.970
and euphoria.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:58.230
It was honestly the best they’d felt in
years.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.930
Perhaps they were wrong about hunting the
witch in here.

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:04.930
Maybe the real anomaly here was a Russian
forest that made you feel awesome when you

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.040
stepped inside.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.940
While the affected agents were giggling away
in their own little la la land, Baba Yaga

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.010
was bringing the pain.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:17.270
With the same freakish speed, strength, and
ferocity that had surprised the hunting party

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:22.920
weeks earlier, the witch was tearing through
MTF Epsilon-6, ripping through hardened tactical

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:25.650
armor with her long claws and teeth.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:32.350
She took shot after shot, enough tranquilizer
to put down an elephant, but she kept fighting.

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:36.040
In the end, the training and numerical superiority
of the task force won out.

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:42.260
They were able to secure and contain the Baba
Yaga, soon redesignated SCP-352, and take

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:46.240
it to a nearby Foundation containment site
for further studies.

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:50.270
There they officially recorded all the details:
From the creature’s incredible speed and

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:55.900
strength to its regenerative ability so extensive
that it could even survive being decapitated

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:56.900
and burned.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:59.760
But what about the hallucinogenic effects?

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:05.150
Like a hungry spider, the Baba Yaga’s true
power comes in her ability to spin a deadly

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:06.150
web.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:11.670
Her body is able to produce long, thin, hair-like
fibers, each one coated in powerful hallucinogenic

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:16.510
enzymes that induce a sense of placid, euphoric
stillness in its victims.

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:20.570
When it isn’t engaging multiple targets,
the creature can sometimes take multiple days

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:25.950
to consume a single, still-living victim,
taking them apart and eating them piece by

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.160
piece.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:33.190
Speaking of eating: As you can probably imagine,
in order to keep SCP-352 uneventfully contained,

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:36.070
it’s ideal to make sure it isn’t hangry.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:41.530
In order to keep 352 well-fed, they need to
stock up on its favorite food, human flesh.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:46.730
Though specifically, 352 has a real hankering
for babies.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:51.210
While the Foundation are currently exploring
anomalous means of keeping the Baba Yaga fed,

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:55.980
until those means are fully ironed out, they
need to keep this monster fed the old-fashioned

00:11:55.980 --> 00:12:01.700
way - only ever withdrawing food as punishment
if it attempts to breach containment.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:06.690
After all, there’s a very good reason why
parents and children across the Slavic world

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:08.460
fear Baba Yaga.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:15.250
She’s always hungry, and in the end, she
always gets what she wants...

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:20.750
Now go check out “SCP-3999 - I Am At The
Center of Everything That Happens To Me”

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:26.030
and “Waldo Finds You - SCP-4885 - Find Him”
for more of the most frightening anomalies

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:26.670
out there!

